# installer/strip-hooks-allowlist — CONF-10 S2 audit
#
# Each non-empty, non-# line names ONE installer-chroot hook that we
# intentionally strip post-unpack because its `apt-install <X>` targets
# a Debian-specific package not present in our pool:
#
#   <hook-path-glob>\t<reason>
#
#   hook-path-glob  fnmatch-style glob, matched against the chroot-
#                   relative posix path of the hook file
#                   (e.g. `usr/lib/pre-pkgsel.d/20install-hwpackages`).
#   reason          Free-text rationale.  Surfaces in build log
#                   when the strip applies.
#
# A hook whose apt-install targets are all in our pool needs no entry
# here — it stays in the chroot.  A hook whose targets miss the pool
# and which is NOT here aborts the build (the gate replacing the
# rotting hardcoded list in installer_chroot.py).

# hw-detect ships /usr/lib/pre-pkgsel.d/20install-hwpackages that runs
# `apt-install discover` — Debian's hardware-detection DB used by
# discover-pkginstall.  We don't ship discover; the install hook
# fails with "Unable to locate package discover".  Strip.
usr/lib/pre-pkgsel.d/20install-hwpackages	hw-detect → discover (Debian hardware-detection DB not in pool)

# save-logs ships /usr/lib/pre-pkgsel.d/50save-logs that runs
# `apt-install installation-report` — Debian's BTS install-report
# submission tool.  We don't ship it; the hook fails with locator error
# and would generate log spam.  Strip.
usr/lib/pre-pkgsel.d/50save-logs	save-logs → installation-report (Debian BTS tool not in pool)

# rootskel ships /usr/lib/finish-install.d/07rootskel with a
# `apt-install compiz` line inside `if /bin/in-target dpkg -l
# mate-session-manager`.  Compiz is the legacy MATE window
# compositor used for the dark-theme accessibility path; we don't
# ship MATE so the guard never satisfies at install time.  The
# audit greps statically and can't see the guard — strip rather
# than fork the udeb (upstream layout may shift across releases).
usr/lib/finish-install.d/07rootskel	rootskel → compiz (MATE dark-theme path; we don't ship mate-session-manager)

# brltty ships /usr/lib/finish-install.d/07brltty with a
# `apt-install brltty 1>&2` line inside `if [ -r $pid ] && kill -0
# $(cat $pid)` — fires only if a brltty daemon was running during
# install (i.e., the brltty udeb was present in the installer
# ramdisk).  We don't ship the brltty udeb (accessibility is
# deferred until INST-02), so the guard never satisfies.  Revisit
# this entry when INST-02 lands and brltty is in the udeb closure.
usr/lib/finish-install.d/07brltty	brltty → brltty (accessibility path; we don't ship brltty udeb — revisit when INST-02 lands)
